acknowledge, resolve; ",[253,353,354],{},"dedup_key"," = incident name",[235,357,358],{},"Routing Key*, Events API URL",[188,360,361],{},"* Password field: stored encrypted, shown as asterisks.",[206,363,365],{"id":364},"who-hears-what","Who hears what",[367,368,369,379,393,399,402],"ul",{},[370,371,372,373,375,376,378],"li",{},"Opened and reopened incidents go to the ",[192,374,101],{},"; escalations to the ",[192,377,197],{},".",[370,380,381,382,384,385,388,389,392],{},"When someone acknowledges or resolves an incident (Desk or a signed link), ",[192,383,348],{}," channels\nalways get the matching ",[253,386,387],{},"acknowledge"," \u002F ",[253,390,391],{},"resolve"," event, so the alert closes on call too.",[370,394,395,396,378],{},"The other channels hear a resolution only when the rule has ",[192,397,398],{},"Notify On Resolve",[370,400,401],{},"A test from the rule form triggers then resolves on PagerDuty, so it never leaves an alert open.",[370,403,404,405,409],{},"During a ",[258,406,408],{"href":407},"\u002Falerts\u002Frules#maintenance-windows","maintenance window",", notifications wait until it ends.",[206,411,413],{"id":412},"signed-action-links","Signed action links",[188,415,416,417,388,420,423,424,427,428,431],{},"Alerts for unresolved incidents carry signed ",[192,418,419],{},"Acknowledge",[192,421,422],{},"Resolve"," links, valid 24 h\n(",[192,425,426],{},"Wolf Settings → Action Link Hours","). Opening a link shows a confirmation page; only its button\nacts, so mail scanners cannot acknowledge for you. Security incidents also carry a link per\n",[258,429,430],{"href":81},"response action"," Wolf proposes; those ask for a Wolf Manager's login.",[206,433,435],{"id":434},"delivery-status","Delivery status",[188,437,438,439,442,443,446],{},"Every attempt is recorded as a ",[192,440,441],{},"Wolf Delivery",": channel, target without secrets, kind, PagerDuty\naction, ok or error, HTTP status. The incident lists them under ",[192,444,445],{},"Deliveries",". Deliveries follow\nthe event retention.",[206,448,450],{"id":449},"upgrading-from-01","Upgrading from 0.1",[188,452,453,454,457,458,462,463,467],{},"Digests were removed in 0.2: every channel sends each alert at once. A channel that used hourly\ndigests in 0.1 now gets every alert as it happens. Digests still pending at the upgrade are\ndropped, not sent: the upgrade prints how many and records the count in an ",[192,455,456],{},"Error Log"," titled\n",[459,460,461],"em",{},"Dodock Wolf 0.2: pending digests dropped",". Release ",[258,464,466],{"href":465},"\u002Fgetting-started#staying-on-v010","v0.1.0","\nkeeps digests.",[206,469,471],{"id":470},"setup-per-type","Setup per type",[473,474,475],"collapsible",{"name":280},[188,476,477,478,481,482,485,486,489],{},"Create an app → ",[192,479,480],{},"Incoming Webhooks"," → ",[192,483,484],{},"Add New Webhook to Workspace",", and paste the\n",[253,487,488],{},"https:\u002F\u002Fhooks.slack.com\u002Fservices\u002F…"," URL. Buttons open the incident or the signed action page, so no\nSlack interactivity endpoint is needed. Slack may show a warning icon on link buttons of apps\nwithout one.",[473,491,492],{"name":291},[188,493,494,497,498,501],{},[192,495,496],{},"Integrations → Incoming Webhooks → Add",", and paste the ",[253,499,500],{},"https:\u002F\u002F…\u002Fhooks\u002F…"," URL.",[473,503,504],{"name":301},[188,505,506,507,510,511,514,515,518,519,522,523,378],{},"Create a bot account, invite it to the room and join. Get its access token (Element: ",[192,508,509],{},"Settings →\nHelp & About → Access Token",", or ",[253,512,513],{},"POST \u002F_matrix\u002Fclient\u002Fv3\u002Flogin","). The Room ID is the internal\n",[253,516,517],{},"!…:server"," one (",[192,520,521],{},"Room settings → Advanced","), not an alias. Messages are sent with\n",[253,524,525],{},"PUT \u002F_matrix\u002Fclient\u002Fv3\u002Frooms\u002F{room}\u002Fsend\u002F…",[473,527,528],{"name":315},[188,529,530,531,534],{},"Any topic on ntfy.sh or your own server. On a public server, pick an unguessable topic, or protect it\nand paste an access token (",[253,532,533],{},"tk_…","). Priority: critical 5, warning 4, info 3, resolved 2; escalations\none step higher.",[473,536,537],{"name":326},[188,538,539,542],{},[192,540,541],{},"Apps → Create application",", and paste its token. Priority: critical 8, warning 5, info 3,\nresolved 2; escalations two steps higher.",[473,544,545,568,571],{"name":337},[188,546,547,548,551,552,555,556,559,560,563,564,567],{},"Provider agnostic. The Gateway URL and the optional Body Template take ",[253,549,550],{},"{to}",", ",[253,553,554],{},"{text}"," and\n",[253,557,558],{},"{secret}"," placeholders: URL-encoded in the URL and form bodies, JSON-escaped in JSON bodies. The Auth\nHeader is a header line such as ",[253,561,562],{},"Authorization: Bearer {secret}",". Put API keys in ",[192,565,566],{},"Secret",", never\nin the URL. One request per phone number.",[188,569,570],{},"The text (kind, severity, title, scope, and the incident URL when it fits) is folded to the GSM-7\nalphabet and cut on a word boundary to 160 characters (one SMS) or 306 (two). Text that needs\nUnicode fits 70 \u002F 134.",[572,573,580],"pre",{"className":574,"code":576,"filename":577,"language":578,"meta":579},[575],"language-text","Gateway URL:   https:\u002F\u002Fsms.example.com\u002Fapi\u002Fsend\nMethod \u002F Body: POST, json, {\"to\": \"{to}\", \"message\": \"{text}\"}\nAuth Header:   Authorization: Bearer {secret}\n","A gateway that takes JSON","text","",[253,581,576],{"__ignoreMap":579},[473,583,584],{"name":348},[188,585,586,587,590,591,594],{},"Add an ",[192,588,589],{},"Events API v2"," integration to a service and paste its integration key as the Routing Key.\nChange the Events API URL for the EU region (",[253,592,593],{},"https:\u002F\u002Fevents.eu.pagerduty.com\u002Fv2\u002Fenqueue","), or for an\nEvents-v2 compatible receiver: Grafana OnCall, Opsgenie and others accept the same body.",{"title":5